---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How ImgThemer handles your images and personal data: conversion on a server in Germany, no image storage, your saved theme and cookieless Umami analytics."
>
  <section>
    <h1 class="section-heading">Privacy policy</h1>

    <p class="date">Last updated: 3 November 2026</p>

    <p>
      ImgThemer is a free hobby project. It sets no cookies and loads fonts,
      images and scripts from its own server in Germany. Your images are only
      used to create the themed version you asked for and are never kept. Apart
      from the providers named below, nothing is passed to third parties such as
      Google, ad networks or social networks.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      Mikayil Gacek<br />
      Mühlstr. 32<br />
      65760 Eschborn, Germany<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:mikayil_gacek@icloud.com"
        >mikayil_gacek@icloud.com</a
      >
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      ImgThemer runs on a server of Hetzner Online GmbH, Industriestr. 25, 91710
      Gunzenhausen, Germany, in a data centre in Germany. To deliver a page, the
      server processes technically necessary connection data such as your IP
      address, the date and time of the request, the requested page, the
      referring page and information about your browser and operating system.
      The web server keeps no log of page views. The legal basis is my
      legitimate interest in delivering this website securely and reliably (Art.
      6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>Your images</h2>
    <p>
      Choosing an image only shows a preview in your browser. When you pick a
      palette, the image and its file name are sent over an encrypted connection
      to the server, converted there and sent back to your browser. This happens
      again for every palette you try. The original and the converted file exist
      on the server only during the conversion and are deleted right after it.
      Nobody looks at them, and they are not passed on or used for anything
      else. Please only upload images you are allowed to use. The legal basis is
      providing the service you asked for (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>Your theme setting</h2>
    <p>
      ImgThemer saves whether dark mode is on in your browser's local storage (<code
        >dark-mode</code
      >). It does this when you use the theme switch, and on your first visit
      when your device is set to a dark theme, so the page keeps that look. The
      value never leaves your browser, and you can delete it in your browser
      settings at any time. It is used for nothing but showing the page in the
      right theme (Section 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics with Umami</h2>
    <p>
      To see how ImgThemer is used, I use the open-source software Umami. It
      runs on my own server in Germany, sets no cookies and creates no profiles
      across websites. It records the page viewed with its title and time, the
      referring page, browser, operating system, device type, screen size,
      language and the approximate location (country, region, city). From your
      IP address and browser details Umami computes an ID that changes every
      month, so repeat visits within a month count once. For each conversion the
      server also reports to Umami whether it started, finished or failed, with
      a random ID, the file type and the chosen palette; for a failure also the
      reason, the file size if the file was too large, or the submitted palette
      name if it was invalid. With these reports the server passes on your
      browser's user agent and the referring page, but never the image itself.
      Your IP address is processed only briefly and is not stored. The analytics
      data is deleted automatically 24 months after it was collected. The legal
      basis is my legitimate interest in a privacy-friendly evaluation and
      improvement of this website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>Contact by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to me by email, your address and message are stored in my
      mailbox at Apple iCloud, run by Apple Distribution International Ltd.,
      Hollyhill Industrial Estate, Cork, Ireland. Apple may also store them in
      the USA and bases such transfers on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses. I
      use your address and message only to answer you and delete them once your
      request is settled, unless the law requires me to keep them. The legal
      basis is my legitimate interest in answering your request (Art. 6(1)(f)
      GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>
      Links to GitHub, X and other websites are plain links. Data only reaches
      these services when you click a link, and from then on their own privacy
      policies apply.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access your data, to have it corrected or erased, to
      restrict its processing, to data portability and to object to processing
      based on legitimate interests (Art. 15 to 18, 20 and 21 GDPR). Just write
      to the email address above. You can also complain to a data protection
      supervisory authority, for example the one responsible for me: Der
      Hessische Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit,
      Gustav-Stresemann-Ring 1, 65189 Wiesbaden, Germany.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style lang="scss">
  section {
    max-width: 800px;

    h2 {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    p {
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--primary);
    }
  }
</style>
